From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:49:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 33/39] Servers: memory given back after a busy place
 (IbashoTrimMemory)

On Second Life a viewer that had been in a crowded region stayed at that
size after leaving (5.7 GB at a quiet corner, from 2.3 GB before): glibc
keeps freed memory for reuse instead of handing it back. On Linux, every
IbashoTrimMemory seconds (0, never, by default; Ibasho's tools set it on
servers) malloc_trim gives the free pages back, between frames.
